  <i class='prompt-icon icon-question-mark'></i>
  <div class="content" >
    <div class="question" data-action="./click-_collapse" aria-controls="faq-answer_element_3011126">
      Display does not work on initial power but does work after a reset.
    </div>

    <div id="faq-answer_element_3011126" data-collapse-target="content" class="answer collapse">
      <p>The OLED driver circuit needs a small amount of time to be ready after initial power. If your code tries to write to the display too soon, it may not be ready. It will work on reset since that typically does not cycle power. If you are having this issue, try adding a small amount of delay before trying to write to the OLED.</p>
<p>In Arduino, use <strong>delay()</strong> to add a few milliseconds before calling <strong>oled.begin()</strong>. Adjust the amount of delay as needed to see how little you can get away with for your specific setup.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
